meta {
  name: Android First Chat Visual Counterpart
  type: folder
  seq: 7
}

docs {
  Use this folder to simulate the other participant while the Android emulator drives the real/current user.

  Assumptions:
  - Backend is running with local-nodb or local-postgres so DevAutoAuthFilter accepts X-Dev-User-Id.
  - The Android user already has an ACTIVE profile and is queued from the app.
  - Optional: set androidUserId in the Bruno environment. If set, the process request verifies the created match contains that user.

  Typical flow:
  1. Android app enters matchmaking room and calls POST /api/matchmaking/queue.
  2. Run 00-08 in this folder to create/enqueue the counterpart and process matchmaking.
  3. Android app polls GET /api/me/home and should see activeMatches[0].
  4. Run 09-14 to make the counterpart send/approve first chat and approve visual review.

  If the backend is local-firebase, these local-dev/X-Dev-User-Id requests will not work. Use a second Firebase test user instead, or add a dev-only fixture endpoint guarded by local profiles.
}
